notes.content:
Yeah, you read that right! After two years, the game was remade.

Why?
This is my dream game, and I don't want it to be a bad game. Making it using Unity 5 was a bad experience (also very buggy 'cause engine limitations) and, after a long time thinking, I decided to remake this game in my own engine.

What changed?
If we're going to remake something, why keep it the same as the old version? The new version have some changes:

Some new arts;
New worlds and levels (fewer levels, but better level design);
More polishing;
New achievements were added, some were removed;
No more double jump (too OP).


I hope you guys enjoy the new version as much as I do. See ya!
